leverage: 24
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(20) x split_weight(1) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  On audience primacy — which reader the artifact is shaped for when the two
  conflict: a person reading it, or a parser consuming it — the records assert
  both machine addressability first (8 judgments, 0 authored) and human
  readability first (12 judgments, 7 authored). Which should be the stated rule,
  and where is the exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

